Well, why don't we take a break?
好吧，我们要不要休息一下？

302
00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:47.420
And then we come back.
然后我们再回来。

303
00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:49.800
We will start breaking down The Matrix.
我们将开始解析《黑客帝国》。

304
00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:50.840
Yes.
好的。

305
00:14:51.040 --> 00:15:00.120
And you guys, I have a really fun The Office crossover to The Matrix, thanks to some deleted scenes from the finale that Dave Rogers helped me find.
各位，多亏了戴夫·罗杰斯帮我找到的一些大结局删减片段，我有一个非常有趣的《办公室》与《黑客帝国》的联动内容。

306
00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:01.180
We'll be back.
我们马上回来。

307
00:15:07.770 --> 00:15:11.130
Attention all new and existing members of the WDNC.
请注意，所有WDNC的新老成员。

308
00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:14.970
I'm Melanie Sanders, and this is the We Do Not Care Club podcaSt.
我是梅兰妮·桑德斯，这里是“我们不在乎俱乐部”播客。

309
00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:19.230
We got to midlife and realized we just simply do not care much anymore.
我们到了中年才意识到，我们真的没那么在乎了。

310
00:15:19.470 --> 00:15:27.310
Now, we got to help each other make sense of hot flashes, itchy ears, chin hair, trifling families, brain fog, and bat wings.
现在，我们要互相帮助，去理解潮热、耳朵发痒、下巴长毛、琐碎的家庭事务、脑雾和蝴蝶袖这些问题。

311
00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:30.170
We are not alone, and we will be heard.
我们并不孤单，我们的声音会被听到。

312
00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:32.090
So come join the WDNC.
所以，快来加入WDNC吧。

313
00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:37.470
Follow and listen to the We Do Not Care Club podcast with Melanie Sanders wherever you get your podcaSt.
在各大播客平台关注并收听梅兰妮·桑德斯的“我们不在乎俱乐部”播客。

314
00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:40.980
All right, we are back.
好了，我们回来了。

315
00:15:41.220 --> 00:15:44.000
As you guys know, The Matrix came out in 1999.
如你们所知，《黑客帝国》是在1999年上映的。

316
00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:48.580
I wanted to share with you that I saw this movie opening weekend.
我想和你们分享的是，我在首映周末就看了这部电影。

317
00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:54.080
I went with a huge group of friends, both from my improv and sketch comedy classes.
我和一大群朋友一起去的，他们都是我即兴表演和素描喜剧课上的同学。

318
00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:55.180
We all went as a group.
我们是一起去的。

319
00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:57.500
We saw it at Man's Chinese Theater in Hollywood.
我们在好莱坞的曼恩中国剧院看的。

320
00:15:57.800 --> 00:16:02.380
And at Man's Chinese Theater at this time, you didn't get assigned seats with your ticket.
那时候在曼恩中国剧院，买票是不指定座位的。

321
00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:04.280
You know, you had to line up outside.
你知道，你得在外面排队。

322
00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:06.720
And the line went outside and around the corner.
队伍一直排到了外面，绕过了街角。

323
00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:09.580
And we went early to stand in line.
我们很早就去排队了。

324
00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:11.900
And there was just such this buzz.
当时那种气氛真是太热烈了。

325
00:16:12.060 --> 00:16:14.800
And our tickets were like for like the 11 o'clock screening.
我们的票好像是11点那场的。

326
00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:16.260
It was like the late screening.
那是场深夜放映。

327
00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:18.180
It was totally sold out.
票完全卖光了。

328
00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:19.780
And I'll just never forget the moment.
我永远不会忘记那一刻。

329
00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:26.720
And there's one thing I'm going to share later when we get to like something that happened in the theater when something happened on screen.
有一件事我稍后会分享，当我们聊到电影里发生某个情节时，影院里也发生了一件事。

330
00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:33.260
But just the buzz, like you said, Jenna, like seeing the green Warner Brothers logo, being in that full crowd.
但就像你说的，珍娜，那种热烈的氛围，看到绿色的华纳兄弟标志，身处满座的观众席中。

331
00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:34.980
We had no idea what to expect.
我们完全不知道会看到什么。

332
00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:38.420
No one had seen this kind of movie making or technology.
没人见过这种电影制作手法或技术。

333
00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:39.680
And I think about that.
我常想起这一点。

334
00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:44.140
We all have movies that we went and saw at the theater that you will never forget.
我们每个人都有那种在电影院看过、永远不会忘记的电影。

335
00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:45.900
And that was this one for me.
而对我来说，就是这一部。

336
00:16:46.160 --> 00:16:49.120
Yeah, you know, for me, that movie is Jurassic Park.
是啊，对我来说，那部电影是《侏罗纪公园》。

337
00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:50.060
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

338
00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:52.340
I saw it by myself in a theater.
我是自己一个人去电影院看的。

339
00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:55.860
I was doing summer stock theater in Kansas.
当时我在堪萨斯州参加夏季剧团演出。

340
00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:57.240
And I had a day off.
我那天正好休息。

341
00:16:57.420 --> 00:17:00.580
And I was like, I want to see this movie everyone's talking about.
我就想，我要去看这部大家都在谈论的电影。

342
00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:01.780
Oh, my God.
天哪。

343
00:17:01.780 --> 00:17:03.840
It scared the bejesus off me.
它把我吓得魂飞魄散。

344
00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.760
And the effects were so cool.
而且特效太酷了。

345
00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:09.360
But, yes, I love that this was one of those movies for you.
但是，是的，我很高兴这部电影对你来说有这样的意义。

346
00:17:10.040 --> 00:17:13.900
Well, listen, Anne, you played the beginning of this movie in our top of show.
好吧，听着，安，你在节目开头播放了这部电影的开头片段。

347
00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:16.120
Here's what's going to happen.
接下来会发生这样的事。

348
00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:23.680
After you hear that little conversation, we see armed men who are going to, like, start flooding a dark hallway.
听完那段简短的对话后，我们看到武装人员开始涌入一条黑暗的走廊。

349
00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:25.440
They're after someone.
他们在追捕某人。

350
00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:29.500
They bust open the store, and we see this woman.
他们破门而入，然后我们看到了这个女人。

351
00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:31.560
From the back, sitting at a chair.
从后面看，她坐在椅子上。

352
00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:35.080
Yes, facing the wall, dressed in head-to-toe leather.
是的，面朝墙壁，从头到脚穿着皮衣。

353
00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.640
They tell her to put her hands up, and she does.
他们叫她举起手来，她照做了。

354
00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:39.780
She's about to open a can of whoop-ass.
她准备要大开杀戒了。

355
00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:40.680
She is.
没错。

356
00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:43.260
Well, this is one of my favorite moments.
嗯，这是我最喜欢的片段之一。

357
00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:48.180
When we go outside, and there's all these special agents who have arrived, and they're talking to cops.
当我们走到外面，看到所有赶到的特工正在和警察交谈。

358
00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:49.340
We don't know who anybody is.
我们不知道谁是谁。

359
00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:50.480
We don't know if she's good.
我们不知道她是好人还是坏人。

360
00:17:50.660 --> 00:17:51.760
We don't know if she's bad.
我们不知道她是好人还是坏人。

361
00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:54.200
Jurisdiction my ass.
管辖权个屁。

362
00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:55.980
He said something like that.
他当时说了类似的话。

363
00:17:56.180 --> 00:17:58.020
The old cop, the agent's like, um.
那个老警察，特工当时大概是，嗯。

364
00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:01.300
Yeah, he's like, I think we can handle one little girl.
对，他说，我想我们能对付一个小女孩。

365
00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:04.420
And the special agents are like, no, lieutenant.
然后特工们说，不，中尉。

366
00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:06.940
Your men are already dead.
你的人已经全死了。

367
00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:11.100
And then it cuts to her, and she is kicking everyone's ass.
镜头切到她，她正在把所有人打得落花流水。

368
00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:18.540
I need to point out, three minutes, 21 seconds, her high kick that knocks the man out behind her?
我得指出，在3分21秒时，她那个把身后男人踢晕的高踢腿？

369
00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:24.280
Yeah, she kicks to the front, but it's like she kicks over her shoulder into his face.
对，她向前踢，但看起来像是越过肩膀踢到了他的脸上。

370
00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:25.560
And hits his head.
踢中了头部。

371
00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:25.820
Yeah.
没错。

372
00:18:25.820 --> 00:18:26.560
He's behind her.
他在她身后。

373
00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:27.200
It's pretty amazing.
这太惊人了。

374
00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:27.800
It's amazing.
确实惊人。

375
00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:33.700
I guess this opening action sequence took six months of training, and it took four days to shoot.
我猜这段开场动作戏花了六个月训练，拍了四天。

376
00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:35.220
Six months, man.
六个月啊，伙计。

377
00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:36.460
Have you ever had to train?
你曾经需要训练过吗？

378
00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:37.800
To do a movie?
为了拍电影？

379
00:18:37.940 --> 00:18:39.040
Have you trained for something?
你为某件事训练过吗？

380
00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:39.780
Look at me.
看看我。

381
00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:41.140
But I mean, anything.
我是说，任何事情。

382
00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:41.460
Look at me.
看看我。

383
00:18:41.740 --> 00:18:42.140
Anything.
任何事情。

384
00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:43.180
5-1.
5比1。

385
00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:44.240
I don't know.
我不知道。

386
00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:47.460
I had to learn how to ice skate for Blades of Glory.
为了拍《荣誉之刃》，我得学习滑冰。

387
00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:48.680
That's a kind of training.
那也算是一种训练。

388
00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:52.360
I learned guitar for Walk Hard, even though I never played in the movie.
为了《永不止步》，我学了吉他，尽管我在电影里从没弹过。

389
00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:52.760
Yeah.
是啊。

390
00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:55.260
Have you ever learned a skill or trained?
你有没有学过什么技能或进行过训练？

391
00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:57.400
I had to make a lot of ham sandwiches.
我得做很多火腿三明治。

392
00:18:59.140 --> 00:19:00.500
For what project?
为了什么项目？

393
00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:02.240
My Hallmark Christmas movie.
我的Hallmark圣诞电影。

394
00:19:02.460 --> 00:19:05.660
We had like a sandwich line, like an assembly line.
我们当时有个三明治生产线，就像流水线一样。

395
00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:07.820
So, do you make a great ham sandwich now?
所以，你现在做火腿三明治很厉害吗？

396
00:19:07.900 --> 00:19:09.460
I mean, better than in the movie.
我是说，比电影里做得好。

397
00:19:09.820 --> 00:19:14.660
Is your ham sandwich as good as Carrie Ann Moss's kick to the guy in the head?
你的火腿三明治有凯莉-安·莫斯踢那个人头部的动作那么厉害吗？

398
00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:15.820
Like, is it comparable?
就是说，有可比性吗？

399
00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:18.220
I could kick my ham sandwich.
我可以踢我的火腿三明治。

400
00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:20.600
Like, she'd kick that chair and take out three people.
就像她踢那把椅子就能干掉三个人一样。

401
00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:21.660
Amazing.
太棒了。

402
00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:22.860
Amazing.
太棒了。

403
00:19:22.860 --> 00:19:27.320
Well, in this scene, Trinity is going to call Morpheus, and she's going to say, listen,
在这个场景里，崔妮蒂要给墨菲斯打电话，她会说，听着，

404
00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:31.200
the line was tapped, you know, and they're coming for me.
电话被监听了，他们正冲我来。

405
00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:35.040
And he tells her a phone that she's got to get to, right?
然后他告诉她必须赶到某个电话亭，对吧？

406
00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:35.840
Yeah, this phone booth.
没错，就是这个电话亭。

407
00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:36.720
This phone booth.
这个电话亭。

408
00:19:37.080 --> 00:19:41.220
And they are coming for her, and the agents are there, and they're running after her.
他们正在追捕她，特工们就在那儿，紧追不舍。

409
00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:44.020
And she goes flying down this stairway.
她飞快地冲下楼梯。

410
00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:48.460
She lands on her back, and she looks up at the door, just like waiting.
她背部着地摔倒，抬头看着那扇门，仿佛在等待着什么。

411
00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:49.600
Are they there?
他们到了吗？

412
00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:50.640
Are they about to get me?
他们要抓到我了吗？

413
00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:57.180
And she lays there for a minute, and Carrie Ann Moss, in one moment, is so powerful and
她躺在那儿片刻，凯莉-安·莫斯在那一瞬间展现出的力量与

414
00:19:57.180 --> 00:19:57.620
vulnerable.
脆弱感真是绝了。

415
00:19:57.860 --> 00:19:58.280
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

416
00:19:58.480 --> 00:19:59.700
I know the moment you're talking about.
我知道你说的是哪个瞬间。

417
00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:00.000
Yeah.
是啊。

418
00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:03.320
I think about it when she goes, get up, Trinity.
我想到她对自己说“站起来，崔妮蒂”。

419
00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:04.520
Get up.
站起来。

420
00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:09.380
Well, listen, she's going to get to this phone booth on the street, but the agents are going
听着，她本要赶到街上的那个电话亭，但特工们会

421
00:20:09.380 --> 00:20:10.700
to ram it with a truck.
开着卡车撞过去。

422
00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:11.200
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

423
00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:12.340
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

424
00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:13.320
She disappeared.
她消失了。

425
00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:14.100
She got out.
她逃脱了。

426
00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:15.580
We don't know what that means yet.
我们还不知道这意味着什么。

427
00:20:15.820 --> 00:20:20.440
But I remember this opening sequence, and I was like, what the f*** is this movie?
但我记得这段开场戏，当时我就想，这到底是什么鬼电影？

428
00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:21.200
What is happening?
发生了什么？

429
00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:22.140
I am so in.
我彻底被吸引住了。

430
00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:22.620
Right?
对吧？

431
00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:25.080
First of all, it opened with an ass-kicking woman.
首先，开场就是一个超酷的女性角色。

432
00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:25.680
Yeah.
没错。

433
00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:27.920
In some badass-looking pants.
穿着看起来很帅气的裤子。

434
00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:28.420
Yeah.
是啊。

435
00:20:28.980 --> 00:20:31.360
And then all of this, and she disappears.
然后发生了这一切，她就消失了。

436
00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:32.380
Amazing.
太棒了。

437
00:20:32.760 --> 00:20:33.120
Amazing.
太棒了。

438
00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:35.200
Well, now we're going to see more green code.
好了，现在我们要看到更多绿色代码了。

439
00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:35.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

440
00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:40.860
And we're going to go to the small, cluttered apartment of Thomas Anderson, a.k.a.
我们要去托马斯·安德森，也就是尼奥，那间狭小杂乱的公寓了。

441
00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:41.340
Neo.
尼奥。

442
00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:42.020
Yeah.
没错。

443
